{"id": "EUVD-2026-76253", "enisaUuid": "e21d9ae0-6c2c-37d2-a334-b6664dbb1df2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntpm: tpm_i2c_nuvoton: disable IRQ on wait timeout\n\ni2c_nuvoton_wait_for_stat() enables the IRQ before waiting for the\ninterrupt handler to report a status change. If the wait times out, or is\ninterrupted before the handler runs, the function returns without\nbalancing the enable_irq() call.\n\nDisable the IRQ before leaving the failed wait path. Also preserve an\ninterrupted wait's original error code instead of converting it to\n-ETIMEDOUT inside the helper.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/007c9e637e0e0b9d946b7f0e8a42f1f1aca48d7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c9147b2c0d75091ab451c2461d1c91788a7e60b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07c2544a47da481043e945322b1bef71cdd7af79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0dc3f18af01ba9f157b7d810cb22d3752d244ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73e89faee1f9b9119fa70b679058b045168ae633", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cde2d927c29e82380851f209222256c607969a1f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aee2296d09f6aeff41db369c6fd2dcaea3ee302c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/705c4ed0643366963547b2616d53165f2519c81f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6qqr-xmx9-c73w", "CVE-2026-80930"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00b58e65-3ab1-3e19-b413-1eb4b5ca40b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4c336e4b1556f4b722ba597bc6e3df786968a600 <2c9147b2c0d75091ab451c2461d1c91788a7e60b"}, {"id": "07c9fddc-215a-3a5d-81ef-b2d5a8b86297", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "15aeddb8-de4f-38e8-9f2a-43a639c46ee3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "184bd0dc-b1d4-3221-bc31-d2b214bc